FLOWR: a sample that fails to build an RDKit mol reaches
filter_diverse_ligands_bulk as None, and GetMorganFingerprintAsBitVect raises
Boost.Python.ArgumentError on it, aborting the target. It appears only at
larger --sample_n_molecules_per_target (10 was fine, 100 was not).

Dropping them is what the surrounding code assumes -- they can be neither
fingerprinted nor written -- but it also removes them from the output, so the
patch prints the count. FLOWR's own pipeline already resamples for validity
(--max_sample_iter), so this does not change what the model is asked to do; it
does mean FLOWR's reported validity here is over the molecules it could build,
and the dropped count belongs in the caption.

Applied in place under third_party/flowr; see the "[patched]" marker in
flowr/gen/generate_from_pdb.py::filter_diverse_ligands_bulk.
